Per-request disk logging: one human-readable log file per inference
request under REQUEST_LOG_DIR (unset = feature off entirely), containing
the full request, the response written incrementally as it's generated
(so a hung/cancelled/errored request still leaves a trace), and a
performance footer. See REQUEST_LOGGING_SPEC.md (Part 1 for the format,
Part 4 for this port's design/hook points) and request_logging.py (repo
root, standalone — not vendored into this package) for the writer itself.

Both entrypoints get the same shape: gather HTTP-level context once, open
a log file per sub-request, force non-streaming requests onto
RequestOutputKind.CUMULATIVE so the engine actually produces intermediate
RequestOutputs to tap (FINAL_ONLY otherwise yields nothing until the
request is fully done or dead), tap the streaming/non-streaming result
generators for incremental writes, and finalize the log (performance
footer / error block / best-effort partial-footer on cancellation) via
try/except/else/finally around the existing generator loops.

Needs the repo root on PYTHONPATH to import request_logging (see
single-user/start_qwen.sh); degrades to a silent no-op (not a crash) if
it isn't, since the import is wrapped in try/except ImportError.

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < patches/request-logging.patch

Written against vLLM 0.27.1. Reapply after upgrades.
